      "text": "Garden or park. (1) A hill, 1742 feet high, forming the one headland of the coast of Palestine. It is chiefly known in connection with the history of Elijah and Elisha (1 Kgs. 18; 2 Kgs. 2:25; 4:25); also frequently mentioned by prophets (Isa. 33:9; 35:2; Jer. 46:18; 50:19; Amos 1:2; 9:3; Micah 7:14; Nahum 1:4).",
